<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Adolo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1848">1848</a>–<a href="/years/1888">1888</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Oba Adolo</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Adolo was an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oba-dynasty">Oba</a>, or king, of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-empire">Benin Empire</a> in the nineteenth century. According to the empire's profile, he restricted which goods could leave Benin in order to protect the royal monopoly over key export commodities. His policy illustrates the Oba's direct control over trade with Europeans.</p></div>
